  "declared_proposition": "For every nonnegative block-norm matrix B and positive weights u,v, let R=max_i (Bv)_i/u_i and C=max_j (B^T u)_j/v_j. Then ||B||_2<=sqrt(RC). If B is strictly positive, minimizing this bound over all positive u,v gives equality with ||B||_2: positive top left and right singular vectors attain R=C=||B||_2.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Weighted Cauchy-Schwarz gives (Bx)_i^2 <= (Bv)_i sum_j B_ij x_j^2/v_j. Sum in i, use (Bv)_i<=R u_i and (B^T u)_j<=C v_j, and obtain ||Bx||_2^2<=RC||x||_2^2. For a strictly positive matrix, Perron-Frobenius supplies positive singular vectors with Bv=sigma u and B^T u=sigma v, giving equality.",
